{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: journal design Draft 3 exact b2ab1e55712fbcdd1be4de5550c69cd4513976ed, tree 25ab8b37016a0f360d80438de063aace56f21ae8. Scope-only durability and the accepted no-migration/claim-permission decisions are respected.\n\nP1 — Make live establishment acyclic (§16.2).\nThe live ID hashes a seed whose cause is the establishing entry's digest, while that same entry records the live ID. This is an entry-hash → ID → entry-hash cycle. Use an explicitly acyclic cause/derivation, excluding the derived ID from its pre-ID input, or derive the ID after sealing an entry that does not contain it. Native Seed explicitly excludes the creating-entry hash and uses the creating input's digest; sends derives the seed before sealing. The identity witness must construct the real entry and seed, not start with an already constructed circular value. Name the bounded bootstrap descriptor/owned locator from which a storage-free object obtains its host, establishment fact and definition; an opaque hash cannot reveal them. Routing can remain an owned L3 dependency, but the hash cycle must be removed.\n\nP2 — Confirm the receipt at its own position (§15.6/A4).\nSummary.archive.hash belongs to through=N. A receipt at n\u003cN normally has a different hash, so summary-only “at or past ... hashes agree” either rejects ordinary advancement or leaves the receipt's membership unproved. Bind the same full ScopeRef and check the exact seq/hash within the named confirmed commit/prefix. A4 must cover n=N, n\u003cN, wrong incarnation/hash, and unavailable/no archive. Distinguish last-confirmed bookkeeping from fresh remote availability or an externally moved ref. This repairs optional client confirmation; it adds no act acknowledgement barrier.\n\nP2 — Freeze the archive input set for an exact retry (§§15.3–15.5).\nAn entry-bounded pass and “every retained input” give no retained-input cutoff. Native turns can add inputs after Mark or during restart, while the pending row stores only parent/through/CID/time. Re-enumerating current storage can build a different tree. Define an immutable prefix-closed input selection or persist the exact pending manifest/objects before dispatch; include kind/domain/digest and explicit omission coverage. Witness a parent still unupdated, a new input after Mark, then restart/resend of the identical marked commit. Deterministic commit inputs must include parent, cutoff and object format; different parents/batch schedules change Git commit IDs. J2 privacy exclusions remain allowed, with their A1/A3 coverage gate.\n\nP2 — Specify native ref and domain encoding (§15.4/A1/A2).\nNative ScopeId is sc_ plus52 base32 characters, not64 hex. Use that spelling or define/check a canonical digest conversion. Define a safe, reversible path segment encoding for value domains, rather than treating arbitrary native strings as path grammar. An untrusted clone source must resolve the named commit/tree under its bounds and avoid root escape or working-tree/symlink substitution. This does not authorize changing native IDs.\n\nP2 — Bound live traffic's host dependencies (§16.3/§16.4/L5).\nSeparate objects isolate live mutation, but the design explicitly sends authorized host reads across objects. A live flood can consume host/read-authority work; it cannot justify the absolute “cannot delay host turns” claim. Keep bounded/backpressured shared dependencies and a mixed host-read/flood witness. Withdraw the old region scheduler as decided; no old envelope or numerical production proof is requested.\n\nArchitecture/Security/Simplification: one pinned level per scope, zero-durability live generations, no live facts/receipts/history, explicit promotion, and separate observations are coherent directions. Archive remains asynchronous after DO commitment, never strict ACK or publication. Detached text bytes stay absent and replay may be INCOMPLETE. Register/inbox are excluded initially. Claim consent must explain the coarser repository read door; J2 screening and archive-token prefix enforcement remain owned before bytes are exported. J7/new platform versions/no old-room migration are decided. L1–L5/J1–J4 are scoped dependencies, not generic runtime-proof blockers. Explicit level support is prospective; only absent-level existing definitions are built today.\n\nCoverage: primary FIRST logical FULL peers112352B1811LF SHA75e3a9c782bb2f3ab8176209d2ddefe8e2e3dc18d8b4de18f5b0521647ca0e85, via native100823 unchanged bytes from prior FULL D2 plus11529 fresh bytes. FULL U3 peers20343B288LF SHA5f29271a2dc2926128d72692b629ae42d4ab5b925ed7930f7df532afb1965e7d. Both final reports/audits/maps FULL Root; native reconstruction, old24-span ledger and current coverage independently verified. Root own body is PARTIAL overall, with FULL15.2/16 and prior D2Section15; bounded native Seed/ID/sends/field units FULL, whole modules PARTIAL. Audit /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-checker-state/journalD3-root-native-audit.json803B SHA6eb59c09b252b06c7598d3185258c1a8265ee879970606db6bf0b9ba70b18389. No implementation commission, Source/tests/gate/build/provider/browser/private execution. A0–A5/live witnesses UNRUN; full scope retained and demo heads prioritized. Normal prepare assigns0d72/fae/main only.\n","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bcfe68a13c08dd0c569878f60fb8054724d06464","binding":"assigned","head":"b2ab1e55712fbcdd1be4de5550c69cd4513976ed","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:87cf90c7e78fffee815fb0cd6362028abeea4cfd\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fae322e0901ae73e961b1434c6fe55ec6d842b73\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:104832109c87e075fac6831eef683c2ba79e9076","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}